    "details": "<h1>UAV Competition&nbsp;<br />Team Size: 3&ndash;6 members per team&nbsp;<br />Eligibility: Open to all engineering students; safety briefing mandatory before flight rounds&nbsp;<br />Rounds / Format&nbsp;<br />● Round 1 &ndash; Technical &amp; Safety Inspection: UAVs are checked for airworthiness and compliance with safety&nbsp;<br />norms.&nbsp;<br />● Round 2 &ndash; Mission Flight: Teams complete assigned mission tasks (e.g., payload drop, navigation, mapping)&nbsp;<br />within a time limit.&nbsp;<br />● Round 3 &ndash; Documentation &amp; Viva: Teams submit a design report and answer questions from the judging panel.&nbsp;<br />Rules &amp; Regulations&nbsp;<br />● All UAVs must pass the mandatory safety inspection before being allowed to fly.&nbsp;<br />● Maximum takeoff weight and flight altitude limits will be specified in the venue-specific briefing and must be&nbsp;<br />strictly followed.&nbsp;<br />● Flights are permitted only within the designated flight zone; flying over the audience or restricted areas is&nbsp;<br />strictly prohibited.&nbsp;<br />● A minimum of one team member must be a certified/trained pilot or have prior flight experience, subject to&nbsp;<br />organizer verification.&nbsp;<br />● In case of a crash or malfunction, the flight is stopped immediately and safety marshals must be informed.&nbsp;<br />● Teams must carry spare batteries/propellers as backups are not provided by the organizers.&nbsp;<br />Judging Criteria&nbsp;<br />Mission task completion &nbsp;| &nbsp;Flight stability and control &nbsp;| &nbsp;Adherence to safety protocols &nbsp;| &nbsp;Quality of design&nbsp;<br />documentation&nbsp;<br />Grounds for Disqualification&nbsp;<br />● Failing the safety inspection&nbsp;<br />● Flying outside the designated zone&nbsp;<br />● Endangering spectators or property&nbsp;<br />● Unauthorized modifications after inspection</h1>",
